### V-001 — Closing a task before hosted closure

Illustrative only: an existing owning task, already eligible for execution with verified active tracking associations, finishes its result and required checks. In one closing commit, the owner includes that task's remaining result, current evidence and initial unchecked-to-checked transition in its owning list. The subject begins with exactly the existing owning task ID; no second executable task closes there. Inspect the staged boundary and actual committed parent diff. Immediately push that commit to the established branch and verify remote containment before further project work or another commit. After verified committed completion and publication, reconcile the confirmed task issue through sdd-forge; a hosted closure failure remains pending rather than invalidating the verified local result. Required dependent closures and unknown effects still block dependent review or next-phase progression. Milestone closure follows its required review/report task and verified exits, not the task checkbox alone.

This sequence derives from [Task commit contract and Complete and commit each task](../../../../skills/sdd-implement/references/completion-and-checkpoints.md), especially steps 5–7, and [Publish each commit](../../../../skills/sdd-manage/references/git-workflows.md#publish-each-commit). It describes expected ordering; no task, checkbox or hosted object was created or closed in this amendment.

### V-002 — Resuming unresolved publication

Illustrative only: continuation discovers an existing verified task closing commit whose push previously failed or has uncertain effect. Inspect the actual branch/ref, closing subject and parent diff, current evidence and checklist transition; preserve pending files/index and audit only the selected range. Read the established remote to determine whether that exact commit is contained. If absent, finish the existing authorized publication through supported recovery, preserving the commit and stopping advancement while unresolved. If already contained, record readback rather than replaying task implementation or creating another closing commit. Reconcile eligible pending hosted closures only after publication is established. New work may begin only when publication, tracking readiness, dependencies and the selected stopping boundary permit it. A malformed or split closing boundary instead blocks affected advancement for explicit scoped recovery; a forward correction cannot make the original history compliant.

For an existing verified target merge awaiting its push, finish publication of that merge rather than making a duplicate merge. This derives from [Task persistence audit and recovery](../../../../skills/sdd-implement/references/completion-and-checkpoints.md#task-persistence-audit-and-recovery) and [Publish each commit / Continue a blocked workflow](../../../../skills/sdd-manage/references/git-workflows.md). No actual interruption, transport loss, denial or recovery fixture was executed here.

